{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And said</b> — the beginning of the pericope, for the king of Jerusalem is Artaxerxes of Nehemiah, who is called in the Persian language Darius, whom Alexander killed, and now the dominion of Greece began, which extends to this day, as I explained in the book of Daniel, for Greece exiled Jerusalem to Edom, and this is: \"the equipment of a foolish shepherd.\"" "<b>Foolish</b> — like \"cruel.\" And because dominion was cut off and the dominion of Greece came, therefore it is written: \"in the land,\" upon the land of Israel." "<b>And the standing one</b> — that she cannot walk to graze. And all this is the days of exile to this day."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The verse quotation at the end is fragmentary; Ibn Ezra likely cites the phrase כלי רועה אוילי from Zechariah 11:15–16.", 1 "The phrase 'בארץ על ארץ' is obscure; rendered hyper-literally.", 2 "'והנצבה' (the standing one) is feminine singular, referring to an implied staff or flock; rendered literally without resolving the referent."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:53.513423424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}